<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
	Versioned copy of the file 'artemis create' generates, so the JMX/Jolokia roles stay in sync
	with ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE. The generated one is stamped with the role passed to 'artemis create',
	defaulting to 'amq' - a role no user here ever gets.

	WARNING: everything below is INERT, and that is a decision, not an oversight. This authorisation
	guards the Platform MBeanServer, and it is only installed while the JVM's own
	'-Dcom.sun.management.jmxremote' agent is NOT set: that agent creates the MBeanServer during
	startup, before the broker can install the interceptor. artemis.profile sets the flag on purpose,
	because the Prometheus javaagent needs the unguarded MBeanServer to scrape Artemis beans at all.
	Measured: with this file granting a role nobody holds, a console user still read attributes AND
	created an address, both HTTP 200.

	The trade was made knowingly. Read only access to broker state is served by Grafana, off those
	metrics, so the console does not need tiers: it is an administrative tool, and whoever passes the
	HAWTIO_ROLES gate (ARTEMIS_CONSOLE_ROLES, see artemis.profile) is a full administrator. Limiting
	WHICH LDAP groups get in happens there, and that part is enforced. There is deliberately no
	viewer role here, because a role that looks read only but is not enforced is worse than none.

	If a tiered console is ever genuinely needed, the order is: move metrics off the JMX exporter
	onto Artemis' native Prometheus plugin, drop the flag, and only then split these entries by role.
	Dropping the flag on its own silently reduces the Prometheus scrape to zero Artemis series.

	No <connector> element on purpose: remote JMX is not used, so port 1099 stays closed.
-->
<management-context xmlns="http://activemq.apache.org/schema">
	<authorisation>
		<allowlist>
			<entry domain="hawtio"/>
		</allowlist>
		<default-access>
			<access method="list*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
			<access method="get*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
			<access method="is*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
		</default-access>
		<role-access>
			<match domain="org.apache.activemq.artemis">
				<access method="list*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
				<access method="get*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
				<access method="is*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
				<access method="set*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
				<!-- count and browse are needed by the browse tab in the console. -->
				<access method="browse*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
				<access method="count*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
				<access method="*" roles="${ARTEMIS_ADMIN_ROLE}"/>
			</match>
		</role-access>
	</authorisation>
</management-context>
